{"convention":"Sites 0..N-1, open line segment with exterior flux zero. E_j is a bit on edge j,j+1. Every half-layer acts on the even or odd disjoint bonds with real one-occupant rotations [[3,-4],[4,3]]/5 and [[4,-3],[3,4]]/5. A hop toggles its own link. Vacuum has amplitude 1; double occupancy has amplitude 1 unless marked as an alternate contact. Each explicit physical kick is the product of one-link diagonal phases w^E. The main schedule kicks every half-layer. The additional cycles scan kicks after odd half-layers only.","theorem":"The binary defect mask m xor E xor (E<<1) is invariant under a hop and its link toggle and under all local diagonal kicks. In the neutral sector with exterior E=0, every even occupation m fixes E uniquely by prefix parity. For exactly two occupied sites p<q its string is p<=j<q, and sum E=q-p. Restriction by the basis isometry |m> -> |m,flux(m)> gives the exterior-square half-layer followed by w^(q-p). Two occupied sublattices of one coarse cell still have one occupied link, and a blocked bond is stationary. A background E xor flux(m) is static and changes the potential to its Hamming weight. This is an external choice of local dynamics with Gauss constraint, coherent dressed preparation and Born readout, not a derivation of a force on independently set bare particle coordinates.","output_encoding":"Each reported [charge_mask,link_mask,integer_real,integer_imaginary,probability] gives the entire coordinate amplitude divided by the enclosing amplitude_denominator for normalized localized launches. Absent bins vanish. Distinct flux strings orthogonalize different matter configurations under a bare link partial trace. The projected effective amplitudes instead belong to the dressed configuration basis; retaining links permits a gauge-invariant hop analyzer to recombine them. Each snapshot is a possible terminal read on its own realization.","examples":[{"case":"four_sites","sites":4,"field":"idle","contact":1,"initial_charges":[0,2],"in